{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-curated. Not scraped, deliberately: the number that decides a fit is real",
    "memory at a given quant including KV cache, and that is not in anyone's model",
    "metadata. It has to be computed or measured.",
    "",
    "'repo' is the model's home. 'download' is where the weights actually come from,",
    "and for a quantised LLM those are different repos \u2014 pulling the home repo gets",
    "fp16 safetensors, several times the size the fitter budgeted.",
    "",
    "'figures' says how much to trust weights_bytes and kv:",
    "  estimated \u2014 derived from parameter counts and quant ratios",
    "  hub       \u2014 real file sizes and real config.json geometry (run refresh.py)",
    "  measured  \u2014 loaded on this machine and read off nvidia-smi",
    "",
    "quality is a 0-100 judgment call, comparable only within a role.",
    "",
    "'voices' (tts only) lists the selectable voices. Only fixed-voice",
    "models have them - kokoro ships named speakers, so src is the",
    "speaker id (af_ = American female, am_ = American male). Cloning",
    "models have no voice list at all: the reference clip IS the voice.",
    "VoiceDesign takes no clip either - a text description of the",
    "character (character.md) becomes the voice at inference."
  ],
